# Leak-scan denylist, base64-encoded (one value per line, "key=<b64>").
#
# WHY ENCODED: this repo is public. Holding the denylist here in plaintext made
# the gate publish the exact naming scheme it exists to keep out -- one code
# search on this file returned the whole set. Encoding is OBFUSCATION, NOT
# SECRECY: anyone can decode it in one command. What it buys is that the file no
# longer *answers* a grep or a GitHub code search. The authoritative denylist is
# the maintainer-side scan in the Makefile, which is publish-excluded and never
# ships; this copy exists so the public CI gate keeps the same coverage.
#
#   core     : shared by the repo scan (test.yml) and the maintainer publish scan
#   artifact : extra terms scanned only in built sdist/wheel artifacts (publish.yml)
#
# Decode:  sed -n 's/^core=//p' .github/leak-patterns.b64 | base64 -d
# Consumers MUST fail closed on a missing file or an empty decode -- an empty
# ERE matches every line, which reads as "everything is a hit", not "clean".
core=a3ViMFwuKG5ldHxpbyl8azhzLShhdXN8aG5kfGxheHx0b2EpLXwxMFwuKDI1MHw0Mnw0MylcLnwxMDBcLig2NHw2NylcLnwvaG9tZS9bYS16XSsvfCh+fFwkSE9NRSkvKGFuc2libGV8XC5zc2gpfFByb2plY3RzLyhhZ2VudC1tZW1vcnl8QnJhaW4pfGt1YjAtYWk=
artifact=c3luYy1jb3VuY2ls
